'''Rathfriland Rangers Football Club''', referred to as '''Rathfriland Rangers''', or '''"The Whites'''", is a [[Northern Ireland|Northern Irish]] semi-professional football club, playing in the [[NIFL Championship]]. Rathfriland Rangers are a part of the [[Mid-Ulster F.A.|Mid-Ulster Football Association]].<ref>{{Cite web |title=Mid Ulster Football Association |url=https://midulsterfa.co.uk/ |access-date=2025-12-03 |website=midulsterfa.co.uk}}</ref> They compete in the [[Irish Cup]].

The club was managed by former player Ally Wilson from March 2021 to October 2026. During this time, the club experienced an unprecedented era of success, gaining promotion from the NAFL Premier Division to the NIFL Championship, whilst also enjoying numerous Cup successes."}}
